1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:17,603
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-seventh. Today's story is fun: the video game Dragon Quest turns forty years old today. It's one of Japan's most beloved games. Let's listen.

2
00:00:18,204 --> 00:00:34,500
[News] 今日、5月27日は「ドラゴンクエストの日」です。最初のゲームが発売されたのは1986年で、今年で40周年になりました。

3
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:44,847
[News] ドラゴンクエストは日本でとても人気があるゲームです。世界中にたくさんのファンがいます。

4
00:00:45,548 --> 00:00:56,060
[News] 40周年を記念して、ゲーム会社のスクウェア・エニックスはいろいろなイベントやセールを行っています。

5
00:00:56,759 --> 00:01:10,439
[News] ゲームを作った堀井雄二さんは、「40年間、ファンの皆さんに支えられてきました。ありがとうございます」とメッセージを出しました。

6
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:22,036
[News] ドラゴンクエストは勇者が冒険をするゲームです。スライムというモンスターは日本でとても有名です。

7
00:01:22,736 --> 00:01:31,903
[News] 日本では、新しいドラゴンクエストが出ると、会社を休んで遊ぶ人がたくさんいます。

8
00:01:32,603 --> 00:01:40,956
[News] 40年前の小さなゲームが、今では世界中で愛されるシリーズになりました。

9
00:01:41,656 --> 00:01:43,287
[Host] Let's break it down.

10
00:01:43,888 --> 00:01:45,447
[Host] The opening line.

11
00:01:46,048 --> 00:01:57,280
[Slow] 最初のゲームが発売されたのは1986年で、今年で40周年になりました。

12
00:01:58,079 --> 00:02:06,263
[Host] The first game was released in nineteen eighty-six, and this year marks the fortieth anniversary. Let's look at the key words.

13
00:02:06,864 --> 00:02:09,240
[Vocab] 発売

14
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:20,175
[Host] Release, launch. When a new product goes on sale for the first time, you use this word. Not just games. Phones, books, anything.

15
00:02:20,776 --> 00:02:23,008
[Vocab] 周年

16
00:02:23,407 --> 00:02:34,328
[Host] Anniversary. Used with numbers to mark how many years have passed since something started. Tenth anniversary, twentieth anniversary, fortieth anniversary.

17
00:02:34,927 --> 00:02:36,536
[Host] How popular is it?

18
00:02:37,135 --> 00:02:46,544
[Slow] 日本でとても人気があるゲームです。世界中にたくさんのファンがいます。

19
00:02:47,343 --> 00:02:52,024
[Host] A very popular game in Japan, with lots of fans around the world.

20
00:02:52,623 --> 00:02:54,855
[Vocab] 人気

21
00:02:55,256 --> 00:03:04,159
[Host] Popular, popularity. You'll hear this word all the time. A popular restaurant, a popular song, a popular person.

22
00:03:04,759 --> 00:03:07,424
[Vocab] 世界中

23
00:03:07,824 --> 00:03:20,352
[Host] Around the world, all over the world. You take the word for world and add a character that means throughout. You can use the same pattern for other words: all day long, all across Japan.

24
00:03:20,951 --> 00:03:23,159
[Host] Celebrating the anniversary.

25
00:03:23,759 --> 00:03:31,919
[Slow] 40周年を記念して、いろいろなイベントやセールを行っています。

26
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:38,264
[Host] To celebrate the fortieth anniversary, they're holding various events and sales.

27
00:03:38,864 --> 00:03:40,903
[Vocab] 記念

28
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:53,207
[Host] Commemoration, memorial. You'll see this word everywhere in Japan. Memorial stamps, memorial coins, commemorative events. It's always tied to celebrating a moment.

29
00:03:53,807 --> 00:03:55,872
[Host] A message from the creator.

30
00:03:56,472 --> 00:04:01,223
[Slow] ファンの皆さんに支えられてきました。

31
00:04:02,024 --> 00:04:07,135
[Host] I've been supported by all the fans. This is a very emotional line.

32
00:04:07,735 --> 00:04:10,183
[Vocab] 支える

33
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:21,360
[Host] To support. It works for physical support, like holding something up. And also emotional support, like fans supporting a creator for forty years.

34
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:23,951
[Host] What is Dragon Quest about?

35
00:04:24,552 --> 00:04:30,983
[Slow] ドラゴンクエストは勇者が冒険をするゲームです。

36
00:04:31,783 --> 00:04:35,839
[Host] Dragon Quest is a game where a hero goes on an adventure.

37
00:04:36,439 --> 00:04:38,624
[Vocab] 勇者

38
00:04:39,024 --> 00:04:47,639
[Host] Hero, brave person. The first character means courage. The second means person. A person of courage.

39
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,471
[Vocab] 冒険

40
00:04:50,872 --> 00:04:59,728
[Host] Adventure. These two characters together mean to venture into danger. A perfect word for a game about exploring unknown lands.

41
00:05:00,327 --> 00:05:03,040
[Host] And how much Japan loves this game.

42
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:13,192
[Slow] 40年前の小さなゲームが、今では世界中で愛されるシリーズになりました。

43
00:05:13,992 --> 00:05:19,632
[Host] A small game from forty years ago has now become a series loved around the world.

44
00:05:20,232 --> 00:05:22,728
[Vocab] 愛される

45
00:05:23,127 --> 00:05:30,639
[Host] To be loved. The base word means love. In this form, it means to be loved by many people.

46
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:34,240
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

47
00:05:34,839 --> 00:05:51,136
[News] 今日、5月27日は「ドラゴンクエストの日」です。最初のゲームが発売されたのは1986年で、今年で40周年になりました。

48
00:05:51,836 --> 00:06:01,483
[News] ドラゴンクエストは日本でとても人気があるゲームです。世界中にたくさんのファンがいます。

49
00:06:02,184 --> 00:06:12,696
[News] 40周年を記念して、ゲーム会社のスクウェア・エニックスはいろいろなイベントやセールを行っています。

50
00:06:13,396 --> 00:06:27,076
[News] ゲームを作った堀井雄二さんは、「40年間、ファンの皆さんに支えられてきました。ありがとうございます」とメッセージを出しました。

51
00:06:27,776 --> 00:06:38,672
[News] ドラゴンクエストは勇者が冒険をするゲームです。スライムというモンスターは日本でとても有名です。

52
00:06:39,372 --> 00:06:48,540
[News] 日本では、新しいドラゴンクエストが出ると、会社を休んで遊ぶ人がたくさんいます。

53
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:57,591
[News] 40年前の小さなゲームが、今では世界中で愛されるシリーズになりました。

54
00:06:58,291 --> 00:07:01,028
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

55
00:07:01,627 --> 00:07:07,387
[Slow] ドラゴンクエストは何年に発売されましたか？

56
00:07:08,187 --> 00:07:16,012
[Host] What year was Dragon Quest released? Nineteen eighty-six. And today is exactly the fortieth anniversary.

57
00:07:16,612 --> 00:07:19,971
[Slow] スライムは何ですか？

58
00:07:20,771 --> 00:07:27,108
[Host] What is a slime? It's a famous monster from the game. Almost everyone in Japan knows it.

59
00:07:27,708 --> 00:07:36,108
[Slow] 日本では、新しいドラゴンクエストが出ると、どうする人がいますか？

60
00:07:36,908 --> 00:07:42,355
[Host] What do some people in Japan do when a new game comes out? They take the day off work to play it.

61
00:07:42,956 --> 00:07:55,339
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

62
00:07:55,939 --> 00:07:58,196
[News] また明日。
